\description{
Builds adm0/adm1/adm2 population denominators (under-5, under-15, all-ages)
from the raw POLIS Population table. Reduces duplicate \verb{(place, year)} rows
to their median, treats zeros and blanks as missing, flags departures from
district history and fills gaps using district or parent-area estimates.
When \code{worldpop} is supplied, also compares the two sources and uses WorldPop
in the replacement rules described below.
}
\section{Checks and replacement rules}{
Duplicate \verb{(place, year)} values are reduced to their median; conflicting
values are recorded in \code{meta$dup_conflicts}. Zeros and blanks become \code{NA}.
The checks compare each district with its own history (\code{bad_vs_history})
and, when WorldPop is supplied, with WorldPop and province-level ratios
(\code{bad_vs_worldpop}, \code{bad_vs_adm1}). Thresholds control which values are flagged.

Additional checks record unresolved district mappings (\code{meta$orphan_xwalk}),
inconsistent age-band ordering (\code{age_order_bad}), age bands using different
sources (\code{age_source_split}) and unchanged annual values (\verb{<age>_pop_frozen}).
Frozen values are flagged but are not replaced on that basis alone.
With polygon boundaries, \code{wp_implausible} identifies WorldPop estimates
below the configured population-density threshold.
}

\section{Replacing missing or rejected values}{
The reconciled series uses the following sources in order. Interpolation and
rescaling use the district's accepted POLIS values to reduce abrupt changes
caused by switching between population sources.
\enumerate{
\item \strong{\code{polis}}: a POLIS value accepted by the configured checks.
\item \strong{\code{polis_interp}}: linear interpolation between accepted POLIS years.
This step does not extrapolate beyond those years.
\item \strong{\code{worldpop_levelled}}: WorldPop rescaled using the POLIS-to-WorldPop
ratio at the nearest accepted year, when enough paired years are available.
\item \strong{\code{worldpop}}: the unscaled WorldPop estimate when no usable POLIS
level ratio is available.
\item \strong{\code{district_trend} / \code{adm1} / \code{adm0}}: estimates from district trends
or parent administrative areas when the preceding sources are unavailable.
}

Missing and rejected values follow the same replacement rules. The output
retains \verb{<age>_pop_polis} and \verb{<age>_pop_wp} alongside the selected population
so users can compare sources. Passing the checks does not establish that an
estimate is the true population.
}

